{% doc %}
  New in — the drop. The second band the curtain brings up, directly
  under Shop by Age: the newest garments, in real photography, four to
  a row.

  ── Shape ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  head   the same centred emerald eyebrow as Shop by Age — the two bands
         must read as one page — with an optional grey line under it and
         a View-all hand-off to the collection.
  cards  product photography at the catalogue ratio (4:5, §06), serif
         name, serif price. No add-to-cart here: this band's job is the
         invitation, the product page does the selling.

  ── Source ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Admin points it at a collection (New Arrivals). While that collection
  is empty — as it is before the first drop is assigned — the band
  falls back to All products rather than rendering an empty frame, and
  if the store itself has nothing to show the section skips whole.

  Rules kept: tokens only; motion per §08 (transform/opacity, one
  IntersectionObserver, armed by sv-motion-gate as the FIRST child);
  links and the collection come from Admin, never typed here.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign col = section.settings.collection
  if col == blank or col.products_count == 0
    assign col = collections.all
  endif
  assign limit = section.settings.limit | default: 4
-%}

{%- if col.products_count > 0 -%}
<section class="sv-drop sv-amb-host" data-sv>

  {%- render 'sv-motion-gate' -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Ambient ground (sv-system §08c) — the same moving backdrop as the
    band above, so the page reads as one continuous surface.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'sv-ambient' -%}

  <div class="w w--wide">

    <header class="sv-drop__head">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="eyebrow sv-drop__eyebrow" data-sv-motion>{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="sv-visually-hidden">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | default: 'New in' }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.line != blank -%}
        <p class="sv-drop__line" data-sv-motion>{{ section.settings.line }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    {%- comment -%}
      The campaign strip — where the one wide launch frame used to sit.
      One frame said one thing about a drop of several; the strip runs
      two to three narrower frames at a time and scrolls, so the
      campaign photography leads the section instead of competing for a
      cell inside the product shelf (owner's direction, Sep 2026: the
      first-drop portrait moved up here out of the rail).

      Frames come from `campaign frame` blocks. With none set it falls
      back to the two images the section already held — the wide banner
      and the campaign portrait — so nothing is lost on a theme that
      has not been re-edited in Admin. It is a native scroll-snap row:
      a thumb swipes it with no script at all.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign frame_count = section.blocks.size
      if frame_count == 0
        if section.settings.banner
          assign frame_count = frame_count | plus: 1
        endif
        if section.settings.campaign
          assign frame_count = frame_count | plus: 1
        endif
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if frame_count > 0 -%}
      <div class="sv-drop__strip" data-sv-motion>
        {%- comment -%}
          Arrows for a pointer; the row still swipes with a thumb and
          still advances itself. They hide themselves when every frame
          already fits, and each one greys out at its end of the run so
          the strip never pretends there is more to see.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button type="button" class="sv-drop__arrow sv-drop__arrow--prev" data-drop-strip-prev aria-label="Previous campaign frame" hidden>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="sv-drop__arrow sv-drop__arrow--next" data-drop-strip-next aria-label="Next campaign frame" hidden>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="sv-drop__strip-row" data-drop-strip>
          {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
                <a
                  class="sv-drop__frame-slide"
                  href="{{ block.settings.link | default: col.url }}"
                  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
                >
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Slides are as wide as their own picture, so the
                    served rendition is chosen against the row's height,
                    not a column width — a wide frame at 470px tall asks
                    for ~1200px of pixels, and the old 38vw hint fetched
                    a 558px file for it.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 1800 | image_tag:
                    loading: 'lazy',
                    widths: '600,900,1400,1800',
                    sizes: '(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 1200px',
                    alt: block.settings.image.alt | default: block.settings.label
                  }}
                  {%- if block.settings.label != blank -%}
                    <span class="sv-drop__frame-label">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </a>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- if section.settings.banner -%}
              <a class="sv-drop__frame-slide" href="{{ col.url }}">
                {{ section.settings.banner | image_url: width: 1800 | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  widths: '600,900,1400,1800',
                  sizes: '(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 1200px',
                  alt: section.settings.banner.alt | default: section.settings.eyebrow
                }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if section.settings.campaign -%}
              <a class="sv-drop__frame-slide" href="{{ col.url }}">
                {{ section.settings.campaign | image_url: width: 1800 | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  widths: '600,900,1400,1800',
                  sizes: '(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 1200px',
                  alt: section.settings.campaign.alt | default: section.settings.campaign_label
                }}
                {%- if section.settings.campaign_label != blank -%}
                  <span class="sv-drop__frame-label">{{ section.settings.campaign_label }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="sv-drop__shelf">
    {%- comment -%}
      The shelf glides only when it has something to glide for: the
      driver arms the rail when there are more cards than a row holds,
      on a pointer-and-desktop width, outside reduced motion. Hover,
      focus, a hidden tab or the pause roundel all still it (WCAG
      2.2.2); phones always scroll it with a thumb.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sv-drop__grid" {% if section.settings.auto_scroll %}data-drop-rail{% endif %}>
      {%- comment -%}
        The shelf is products only now: the campaign portrait moved up
        into the strip above, where it is read as campaign photography
        rather than mistaken for a garment on sale.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign show = limit -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Two passes: photographed products lead the shelf; anything still
        waiting on its photography joins at the right-hand end, so the
        plain placeholder frames never break up the pictures.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        # dealt counts CELLS on the shelf and doubles as the
        # reveal-stagger index. budget is the row total.
        assign dealt = 0
        assign budget = show
      -%}
      {%- for product in col.products -%}
        {%- if dealt >= budget -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if product.featured_image -%}
          {%- render 'sv-drop-card', product: product, idx: dealt -%}
          {%- assign dealt = dealt | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- for product in col.products -%}
        {%- if dealt >= budget -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- unless product.featured_image -%}
          {%- render 'sv-drop-card', product: product, idx: dealt -%}
          {%- assign dealt = dealt | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The shelf takes the strip's arrows too: it glides on its own, but
      a visitor who wants to look at the next garment now should not
      have to wait for it, and on a phone the row is swiped.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="button" class="sv-drop__arrow sv-drop__arrow--prev sv-drop__arrow--rail" data-drop-rail-prev aria-label="Previous products" hidden>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="sv-drop__arrow sv-drop__arrow--next sv-drop__arrow--rail" data-drop-rail-next aria-label="More products" hidden>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
    </button>

    {%- if section.settings.auto_scroll -%}
      <button class="sv-drop__railtoggle" type="button" data-drop-rail-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Pause the product rail" hidden>
        <svg class="sv-drop__glyph sv-drop__glyph--pause" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M8 5h3v14H8zM13 5h3v14h-3z"/>
        </svg>
        <svg class="sv-drop__glyph sv-drop__glyph--play" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M8 5l11 7-11 7z"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <p class="sv-drop__more" data-sv-motion>
      <a class="act" href="{{ col.url }}">{{ section.settings.cta_label | default: 'View everything new' }}</a>
    </p>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Motion driver — the section family's, verbatim in shape (sv-about,
    sv-shop-by-age). Hidden state exists only under .sv-motion-ready.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    (() => {
      const root = document.currentScript.closest('.sv-drop');
      if (!root) return;
      const targets = root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-motion]');
      if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window) ||
          matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
        targets.forEach(el => el.classList.add('sv-vis'));
        return;
      }
      const io = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
        entries.forEach(e => {
          if (!e.isIntersecting) return;
          e.target.classList.add('sv-vis');
          io.unobserve(e.target);
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.12, rootMargin: '0px 0px -6% 0px' });
      targets.forEach(el => io.observe(el));
      setTimeout(() => {
        targets.forEach(el => {
          const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
          if (r.top < innerHeight && r.bottom > 0) el.classList.add('sv-vis');
        });
      }, 1200);

      /* ── the shelf ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
         A native scroll-snap row, not a transform marquee. The marquee
         moved one card per click behind a 0.7s transition and could not
         be swiped at desktop width: a click felt like waiting for
         something to load, and a trackpad flick did nothing. Scrolling
         the row instead is instant, swipes on every device, and keeps
         the browser's own momentum and back-button behaviour.

         It still drifts on its own — one card every few seconds — and
         still stops for a pointer, a keyboard, a hidden tab, the pause
         roundel, or the moment the reader scrolls it themselves. */
      /* One answer for both rows: 'smooth' unless the visitor asked for
         less motion, in which case the jump is instant rather than
         cancelled. */
      const STILL = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

      /* A scroll we drive ourselves: sets scrollLeft frame by frame, so
         it cannot be dropped by the browser's own smooth-scroll and it
         stops dead the moment someone touches the row. */
      const glideTo = (el, to, ms) => {
        const from = el.scrollLeft;
        const span = to - from;
        if (STILL || !span) {
          el.scrollLeft = to;
          return;
        }
        /* Stepped on a timer rather than requestAnimationFrame: rAF is
           throttled to a standstill while the window is occluded, and a
           glide that never ran left the arrows looking broken. A timer
           still fires, and the row still lands exactly on the target. */
        clearInterval(el._svGlide);
        const started = Date.now();
        el._svGlide = setInterval(() => {
          const t = Math.min(1, (Date.now() - started) / ms);
          const eased = t < 0.5 ? 4 * t * t * t : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * t + 2, 3) / 2;
          el.scrollLeft = from + span * eased;
          if (t >= 1) clearInterval(el._svGlide);
        }, 16);
      };

      const rail = root.querySelector('[data-drop-rail]');
      const railToggle = root.querySelector('[data-drop-rail-toggle]');
      if (rail) {
        const railPrev = root.querySelector('[data-drop-rail-prev]');
        const railNext = root.querySelector('[data-drop-rail-next]');
        let paused = false;
        let touched = false;

        const overflows = () => rail.scrollWidth - rail.clientWidth > 8;

        /* Scroll to a CARD's own left edge rather than by a measured
           step: with mandatory snapping a step that lands a pixel short
           is snapped back where it came from, which is why the arrows
           appeared to do nothing. */
        const cards = () => Array.from(rail.children);

        const edgeOf = (card) => card.offsetLeft - rail.offsetLeft;

        const nextEdge = (back) => {
          const here = rail.scrollLeft;
          const list = cards().map(edgeOf);
          if (!list.length) return here;
          return back
            ? [...list].reverse().find((x) => x < here - 4) ?? 0
            : list.find((x) => x > here + 4) ?? list[list.length - 1];
        };

        const paintArrows = () => {
          const show = overflows();
          [railPrev, railNext].forEach((b) => { if (b) b.hidden = !show; });
          if (railToggle) railToggle.hidden = !show;
          if (!show) return;
          if (railPrev) railPrev.disabled = rail.scrollLeft <= 2;
          if (railNext) railNext.disabled = rail.scrollLeft >= rail.scrollWidth - rail.clientWidth - 2;
        };

        const go = (back) => {
          glideTo(rail, nextEdge(back), 420);
          /* The row's own scroll event can arrive before the glide has
             finished moving, which left an arrow disabled at a position
             it had already left. The ends are re-checked once the glide
             is over. */
          setTimeout(paintArrows, 480);
        };

        if (railPrev) railPrev.addEventListener('click', () => { touched = true; go(true); });
        if (railNext) railNext.addEventListener('click', () => { touched = true; go(false); });

        if (railToggle) {
          railToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
            paused = !paused;
            railToggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(paused));
            railToggle.setAttribute('aria-label', paused ? 'Play the product rail' : 'Pause the product rail');
          });
        }

        /* §08's reveal only lights an element when it crosses the
           VIEWPORT, which a horizontal scroller's later cards never do
           while they sit off to the right: they stayed at opacity 0 and
           arrived blank, which read as the shelf loading on every click.
           Cards in a scroller are revealed with the row itself. */
        const lightCards = () => {
          rail.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-motion]').forEach((el) => el.classList.add('sv-vis'));
        };
        lightCards();

        rail.addEventListener('scroll', paintArrows, { passive: true });
        rail.addEventListener('pointerdown', () => { touched = true; });
        window.addEventListener('resize', paintArrows);
        paintArrows();

        if (!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
          setInterval(() => {
            if (paused || touched || document.hidden || !overflows()) return;
            if (rail.matches(':hover') || rail.matches(':focus-within')) return;
            const end = rail.scrollWidth - rail.clientWidth - 2;
            glideTo(rail, rail.scrollLeft >= end ? 0 : nextEdge(false), 600);
          }, 3600);
        }
      }

      /* The campaign strip advances itself one frame at a time, and
         stops for a pointer, a keyboard, a hidden tab or a reader who
         has scrolled it by hand — the same courtesies the product rail
         takes. With script off it is still a scroll-snap row. */
      const strip = root.querySelector('[data-drop-strip]');
      if (strip) {
        const prev = root.querySelector('[data-drop-strip-prev]');
        const next = root.querySelector('[data-drop-strip-next]');
        const slide = () => {
          const first = strip.firstElementChild;
          const gap = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(strip).gap) || 16;
          return first ? first.offsetWidth + gap : strip.clientWidth * 0.8;
        };
        const paintArrows = () => {
          const over = strip.scrollWidth - strip.clientWidth > 8;
          [prev, next].forEach((b) => { if (b) b.hidden = !over; });
          if (!over) return;
          if (prev) prev.disabled = strip.scrollLeft <= 2;
          if (next) next.disabled = strip.scrollLeft >= strip.scrollWidth - strip.clientWidth - 2;
        };
        if (prev) prev.addEventListener('click', () => glideTo(strip, strip.scrollLeft - slide(), 420));
        if (next) next.addEventListener('click', () => glideTo(strip, strip.scrollLeft + slide(), 420));
        strip.addEventListener('scroll', paintArrows, { passive: true });
        window.addEventListener('resize', paintArrows);
        paintArrows();
      }
      if (strip && !window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
        let touched = false;
        strip.addEventListener('pointerdown', () => { touched = true; });
        setInterval(() => {
          if (touched || document.hidden) return;
          if (strip.matches(':hover') || strip.matches(':focus-within')) return;
          const first = strip.firstElementChild;
          if (!first || strip.children.length < 2) return;
          const gap = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(strip).gap) || 16;
          const step = first.offsetWidth + gap;
          const end = strip.scrollWidth - strip.clientWidth - 2;
          glideTo(strip, strip.scrollLeft >= end ? 0 : strip.scrollLeft + step, 600);
        }, 4200);
      }
    })();
  </script>
</section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Tokens only; rules written .sv-drop .sv-drop__* at (0,2,0) to clear
     the §02 reset, same as sv-shop-by-age. */

  /* Close ranks with the band above — the age chips end 28px up, so
     the two sections read as one page rather than two rooms. */
  [data-sv].sv-drop {
    padding: var(--b) 0 var(--d);
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--c);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__eyebrow {
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: .92rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: .26em;
    color: var(--emerald);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__eyebrow::after {
    content: "";
    width: 44px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--tan);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__line {
    margin: var(--a) auto 0;
    font-size: .95rem;
  }

  /* The campaign strip: two to three narrower frames at a time on a
     native scroll-snap row, so the drop is shown as a set rather than
     one wide picture. Slide width is a fraction of the row, which is
     what makes the next frame peek in and read as scrollable. */
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__strip {
    position: relative;
    margin-block: 0 var(--d, 40px);
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    z-index: 3;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    inline-size: 46px;
    block-size: 46px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cream, #fbf7ef) 92%, transparent);
    color: var(--emerald, #14524a);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.16);
    cursor: pointer;
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
    backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
    transition: opacity 0.18s ease, transform 0.18s ease;
  }

  /* `display: grid` above would out-rank the [hidden] attribute, so an
     arrow asked to hide would stay on screen. */
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow svg {
    inline-size: 20px;
    block-size: 20px;
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow--prev { left: 12px; }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow--next { right: 12px; }

  /* On the shelf the arrows sit against the first row of cards rather
     than the middle of a tall block. */
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow--rail {
    top: 40%;
  }



  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow:hover {
    transform: translateY(-50%) scale(1.06);
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow[disabled] {
    opacity: 0.35;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--emerald, #14524a);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .sv-drop .sv-drop__arrow {
      inline-size: 38px;
      block-size: 38px;
    }
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__strip-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    padding-block-end: 4px;
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__strip-row::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Frames are never cropped: each slide is as wide as its own
     photograph at the row's height, so a wide playroom frame stays wide
     and a portrait stays a portrait. That is what the carousel is for —
     the row scrolls rather than forcing every picture into one window,
     which is how the banner lost its edges before. */
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__frame-slide {
    position: relative;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    block-size: clamp(260px, 34vw, 470px);
    border-radius: 20px;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: block;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--emerald, #14524a) 6%, transparent);
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__frame-slide img {
    display: block;
    block-size: 100%;
    inline-size: auto;
    max-inline-size: none;
    object-fit: contain;
    transition: transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.33, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__frame-slide:hover img {
    transform: scale(1.02);
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__frame-label {
    position: absolute;
    left: 16px;
    bottom: 16px;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--emerald, #14524a);
    color: var(--cream, #fbf7ef);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .sv-drop .sv-drop__frame-slide {
      block-size: 240px;
    }

    .sv-drop .sv-drop__frame-label {
      left: 12px;
      bottom: 12px;
      padding: 8px 14px;
      font-size: 0.66rem;
    }
  }

  /* The campaign portrait keeps its own proportions — a 4:5 crop was
     taking the second child's legs off. The frame follows the image
     instead of imposing the catalogue ratio. */
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__card--campaign .sv-drop__frame {
    aspect-ratio: auto;
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__card--campaign .sv-drop__frame img {
    position: static;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    object-fit: unset;
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__campaign-label {
    position: absolute;
    left: 12px;
    bottom: 12px;
    z-index: 2;
    background: var(--emerald);
    color: var(--cream);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: .6rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: .18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: var(--b);
  }
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .sv-drop .sv-drop__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: var(--c) var(--a);
    }
  }

  /* The shelf as a rail — flex row, clipped, each card a quarter of the
     row so the resting frame matches the grid exactly; the driver only
     arms it past four cards, on desktop, outside reduced motion. */
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__shelf {
    position: relative;
  }
  /* The shelf scrolls at every width: four to a view on a desktop, a
     card and a bit on a phone. */
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__grid {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--b);
    overflow-x: auto;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    padding-block-end: 4px;
  }

  /* No `scroll-behavior: smooth` on either row. On this page a
     programmatic scroll against it never ran at all — the arrows moved
     nothing — so the glide is animated in script instead, where it can
     be seen to work and can be skipped for reduced motion. */

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__grid::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  /* No scroll snapping on either row. Snapping clamps every value a
     scroll passes through, including the frames of an animation, and
     the glide below lands on a card's own edge anyway — the two
     together only fought each other. */
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__grid > * {
    flex: 0 0 calc((100% - (var(--b) * 3)) / 4);
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .sv-drop .sv-drop__grid > * {
      flex-basis: 62%;
    }
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__card {
    display: block;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__frame {
    display: block;
    transition: transform var(--std) var(--e), box-shadow var(--std) var(--e);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-s);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__card:hover .sv-drop__frame {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: var(--sh);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__frame img {
    transition: transform var(--slow) var(--e);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__card:hover .sv-drop__frame img {
    transform: scale(1.04);
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__name {
    display: block;
    margin-top: var(--a);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__card:hover .sv-drop__name {
    color: var(--emerald);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__price {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--emerald);
  }
  .sv-drop .sv-drop__was {
    color: var(--grey);
    margin-right: 8px;
    font-size: .9em;
  }

  .sv-drop .sv-drop__more {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: var(--c);
  }

  /* Motion — armed by the gate, released by the driver, staggered by
     card index. */
  .sv-drop.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion] {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(var(--rise));
    transition: opacity .85s var(--entrance), transform .85s var(--entrance);
    transition-delay: calc(var(--i, 0) * var(--stagger));
  }
  .sv-drop.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

